> ["]Do[zens] of[ network]-attached storage (NAS) servers and other consumer appliances are about to[ gain mainline] kernel and Debian GNU/Linux support. The 2.[6].25[ kernel],[ currently] in the final stages of[ testing],[ will support] Marvell's Feroceon micro-architecture and 'Orion' SoCs,[ with] Debian support close behind,[ sources] say.
